    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a challenging slate today, with our highest-scoring options clustered around moderate-to-difficult pitching matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** (66.87) leads our group, benefiting significantly from a 16% park factor boost that helps mitigate the threat of Shane McClanahan\u2019s elite stuff, despite a negative platoon adjustment. He is closely followed by **Coby Mayo** (62.51), whose profile against the same arm suggests a high-upside play if he can capitalize on the favorable park conditions in his seventh-spot position. **Liam Hicks** (59.92) and **Jackson Merrill** (58.97) round out our top tier; **Liam Hicks** derives significant value from his 16% park boost and a favorable matchup against Brandon Young, while **Jackson Merrill** remains a core start despite his 40% stolen base holding efficiency capping his overall output.\n\nWeather in the games featuring **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Liam Hicks** bears monitoring, with a 34% risk of rain potentially disrupting our most productive bats. On the bench, **Luis Lara** was the most difficult exclusion (47.54), narrowly missing the cut behind **Nasim Nunez** and **Tommy White**. While **Luis Lara** offers switch-hitting flexibility, the optimizer preferred the volume and specific lineup placement of our starters over his bottom-of-the-order profile. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages**, both of whom are projected for steady output despite facing tough arms like Luis Castillo and Jared Jones, respectively. Managers should watch for official lineup cards, as any unexpected drops in batting order will require a reassessment of our efficiency scores for **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci**.",
